    "collapsible_content_NkM9de": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_zMzbxE": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Payment In Advance",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>To ensure that you have secured your booking for a course, please note that payment must be received no less than 5 working days prior to the course start date. </p><p>A spot in our course is only fully secure once payment has been made. </p><p>If the course is cancelled or postponed for more than 4 weeks, we will refund all fees.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_BrJxFF": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Cancellation and Refund Policy",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Regarding cancellations, if a course is cancelled or postponed by more than 4 weeks, all fees will be refunded. To withdraw from a course and receive a full refund, contact our administration office at least five working days before the course starts. If you withdraw within five working days up to 24 hours before the course begins, a 50% refund is available. No refunds are possible for cancellations within 24 hours or for no-shows on the course day. If full payment hasn't been received and a cancellation occurs, EXELTest&Tag Pty Ltd may seek to recover 100% of the course fees.<br/><br/>Online courses are considered to commence once you log in, and no refunds apply.<br/><br/>Refunds will be handled case by case, processed by the Finance and Accounts Department, and based on the original payment method. Refunds take 5 to 10 working days to process and are documented in the student and financial systems. Disputes will be resolved per our Complaints and Appeals policy.<br/><br/>For more information, please view our Refund Policy.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_tLi3M9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Complaints & Appeals Policy and Procedure",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Test & Tag Training believes that a student who has a complaint has the right to raise the complaint and expects that every effort will be made to resolve it in accordance with this policy without prejudice or fear of reprisal or victimisation. The student has the right to present the complaint or appeal informally as well as in writing.<br/><br/>To lodge a complaint or provide feedback, please <a href=\"/pages/contact\" title=\"Contact\">contact us</a> online or submit in writing to:<br/><br/>Test & Tag Training<br/>8 Mosrael Place, Rowville, VIC 3178<br/><br/>To view our full Policy & Procedure, download the <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0861/8482/1048/files/Complaints-Appeals-Policy-Procedure-Mar-2017.pdf?v=1706227650\" title=\"Complaints & Appeals Policy & Procedure - Test & Tag Training\">Complaints & Appeals Policy & Procedure</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
