    "collapsible_content_kpxmdM": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_WMPFcH": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is the course Nationally Accredited?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>As Test and Tag Training is a Registered Training Organisation, this means our Test & Tag Course is of a Nationally Recognised standard.</p><p>We also offer short courses for anyone who’s only looking to meet the minimum requirements of the test and tag industry and isn’t necessarily after the highest qualification.<br/><br/></p><p></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_L8zehg": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are there any renewal requirements for the certification?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>You don’t have to, however, to retain your status as a \"Competent Person\" you MUST have the latest skills and knowledge, as well as keep up to date with the AS/NZS 3760:2022 Standard and any other relevant Codes of Practice. </p><p>The best way to remain competent is to make sure you check the AS/NZS 3760:2022 Standard regularly and complete further training if you feel the need. <br/><br/>We provide an Online Test and Tag Refresher Course which is a great way to ensure you’re completely confident with your testing and tagging skills - and it proves that you’re maintaining an on-going competency which is a requirement.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DpzQqg": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are the benefits of completing the Test and Tag Course?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Completing a Test and Tag Course offers several advantages. </p><ul><li>It enhances safety awareness. This course equips you with the knowledge and skills to inspect electrical appliances and equipment for potential hazards, reducing the risk of accidents such as electric shocks and fires at your workplace.</li><li>It broadens your career prospects. Many businesses and organisations require individuals who can regularly assess and label their electrical devices to ensure a safe working environment. By completing this course, you become a competent person, which is a requirement to conduct any testing and tagging.</li><li>If you are looking to start your test and tag businesses, it’s best to upskill and learn about the test and tag regulations, which can be done through our nationally accredited course.</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_TjRTex": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will I receive a digital or physical certificate?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The certificate you receive depends on the type of course you complete. </p><p>For our short courses, you will receive a digital certificate. </p><p>For our Nationally Recognized courses, you will get both, a physical certificate of completion along with receiving a digital certificate.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
